<title>JAPAN: Mazda March domestic output up 6.9%.</title>
<headline>Mazda March domestic output up 6.9%.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mazda Motor Corp said on Monday its domestic vehicle production, exports, domestic sales and</p>
<p>overseas output in March were as follows (with percentage</p>
<p>changes from a year earlier):</p>
<p> Production	   84,538   up   6.9 percent</p>
<p>  - Cars		66,224   up   3.6 percent</p>
<p>  - Truck &amp; Bus     18,314   up  20.6 percent</p>
<p> Domestic sales     49,918   up  18.5 percent</p>
<p>  - Cars		32,750   up  34.0 percent</p>
<p>  - Truck &amp; Bus     17,168   down 3.0 percent</p>
<p> Exports		47,760   down 2.4 percent</p>
<p>  - Cars		40,609   down 5.3 percent</p>
<p>  - Truck &amp; Bus	7,151   up  17.6 percent</p>
<p>Mazda's domestic vehicle production rose in March for the first time in two months on a year-on-year basis, Mazda said in a statement.</p>
<p>Domestic sales rose for the third successive month on a year-on-year basis.</p>
<p>Exports fell for the first time in six months on a year-on-year basis, the statement said.</p>
<p>Mazda also announced domestic vehicle production, exports, domestic sales and overseas output for the business year ended on March 31, with percentage changes from a year earlier, as follows:</p>
<p>    Production	781,363  up    1.4 percent</p>
<p>  - Cars		596,884  down  1.7 percent</p>
<p>  - Truck &amp; Bus     184,479  up   12.7 percent</p>
<p> Domestic sales     353,685  down  0.6 percent</p>
<p>  - Cars		218,649  up    8.5 percent</p>
<p>  - Truck &amp; Bus     135,036  down 12.5 percent</p>
<p> Exports		463,515  up    8.6 percent</p>
<p>  - Cars		387,578  up    5.2 percent</p>
<p>  - Truck &amp; Bus	75,937  up   29.9 percent</p>
</text>
